---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
const schema = { '@type': 'AboutPage', name: 'Editorial Policy', url: 'https://mushroomscope.com/editorial-policy/', about: { '@id': 'https://mushroomscope.com/#organization' } };
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial Policy" description="How MushroomScope researches, reviews, updates, and corrects mushroom information." schema={schema}>
  <div class="shell py-8"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Editorial Policy' }]} /></div>
  <article class="shell max-w-4xl py-12"><p class="eyebrow">Our standards</p><h1 class="mt-4 font-serif text-5xl">Editorial Policy</h1><div class="prose mt-8"><h2>Research and sourcing</h2><p>We prioritize primary research, systematic reviews, government and university publications, recognized taxonomic databases, and specialist mycological organizations. Commercial pages and unsourced summaries are not used as the sole support for safety, taxonomy, or health claims.</p><h2>Source-to-claim checks</h2><p>A reference is included only when it is relevant to the nearby claim or to the article’s stated scope. Editors check that the cited species, fungal material, preparation, population, outcome, and conclusion match the wording on the page. A long bibliography does not compensate for an unrelated citation.</p><h2>Identification and health content</h2><p>Mushroom identification and health information receives extra scrutiny. We avoid declaring wild mushrooms safe to eat remotely and do not present educational material as medical advice. Laboratory mechanisms, animal experiments, food-composition data, observational studies, and controlled human trials are described as different levels of evidence.</p><h2>Publication requirements</h2><p>A published guide must include an original descriptive image, visible image provenance, topic-specific FAQs, multiple relevant sources, and intentional links to related MushroomScope material. Category-specific structured fields must also be complete before the content system permits publication.</p><h2>Review labels and updates</h2><p>Pages display publication and update dates. Health pages also display the date of their latest editorial or expert review. “Editorially reviewed” means the organizational team checked clarity, source relevance, uncertainty, and safety language; it does not imply review by a clinician, dietitian, or mycologist. Named expert review is shown only when it actually occurred.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Readers can report a possible error through our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Confirmed errors are corrected promptly and the page update date is revised when the change is substantive. Reports should identify the page, disputed statement, and supporting source where possible.</p><h2>Independence and advertising</h2><p>Advertising does not determine our editorial conclusions. Sponsored or affiliate relationships, if introduced, will be clearly disclosed. Advertisers do not receive approval rights over health, identification, or safety language.</p></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
